1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,760
My favorite food? Hmm. Strawberries, I guess.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,620
I see. You have cute tastes, Miss Iona.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:11,320
Hate to say I told you so, but Akira's down in the rankings again.

4
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:15,900
On top of that, she's been ditching work lately. She's really not worth it anymore.

5
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:20,600
Eh, her style doesn't really match her magazine anyway. Kind of their class, you know?

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:24,160
So what should we do about the front page model for the next issue?

7
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,660
What do you think? Drop Akira and go with Yuko?

8
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:32,340
Well, that's just lovely. I wish they'd have their little business talk somewhere else.

9
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:37,120
I like them with some milk and just a pinch of sugar. Is that weird?

10
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,580
Oh, oh, right. Strawberries. Sorry.

11
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:43,340
I always take the backside of my fork and smash them to bits.

12
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:52,400
Just so we're clear, I'm gonna make you apologize.

13
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:54,100
Open!

14
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:58,660
Open!

15
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,660
Open!

16
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:14,260
Open!

17
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:16,060
Oh, right?

18
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:17,460
You know what?

19
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,880
You know what?

20
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:27,400
If you don't have the idea, we must move on like P есть it.

21
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:35,180
führen

22
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:39,060
10

23
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:47,500
11

24
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,440
10

25
00:01:50,440 --> 00:02:18,720
it

26
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:27,420
I'm home.

27
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:29,900
My gosh.

28
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:31,580
What happened, Heatwe?

29
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:33,820
You're soaked to the bone.

30
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,280
Your friends didn't come with you?

31
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:37,460
Did they go home?

32
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,440
Anyway, dry yourself off before...

33
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:45,720
Heatwe?

34
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:55,060
Looks like I'm up first.

35
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:55,860
Aki-laki!

36
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,420
We're gonna school this scrub, Piraluck.

37
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,140
And don't go easy on her just because she's a noob.

38
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,540
Is it okay?

39
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:04,480
What?

40
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,420
Tama will fight to win this.

41
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,700
Of course.

42
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:15,040
I'll draw, drop a card in the inner zone,

43
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,340
have Piraluck grow,

44
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:18,940
and now say hello to Sky Cat.

45
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:20,720
Tama, let's grow!

46
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,960
I summon Kukuri and Monia!

47
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:26,220
You gotta tell your Elric to lay off the coffee.

48
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,540
It's weird.

49
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,360
I've never felt like this.

50
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,160
But battling Akuma is awful.

51
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,120
It's painful.

52
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:35,940
It is painful, but...

53
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,260
I love it!

54
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,620
What the hell?

55
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:41,600
No fair!

56
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,520
I thought she was supposed to be a newbie!

57
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,020
You are correct.

58
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,100
Though she's new to the game,

59
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,980
she takes battle quite seriously.

60
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:49,380
Huh?

61
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:50,940
This is talent.

62
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:53,440
She has a gift.

63
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,520
You trying to tell me something?

64
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:58,040
Why don't you turn around and say it to my face?

65
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:58,640
Huh?

66
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,300
You know what?

67
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:01,000
Screw you!

68
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:02,380
I don't even care anymore!

69
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:05,080
You just keep your mouth shut and do what I tell you!

70
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:05,520
Got it?

71
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,560
Let's get this crap over with quick!

72
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:08,360
Arts!

73
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,680
Time for Peeping Analyze!

74
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,280
Aw, poor Roo Roo.

75
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,920
Now I get to pick a card level,

76
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,040
then all the ones in your hand go bye-bye.

77
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:20,740
And since you dumb rookies love to play by the book,

78
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,500
there's only one answer.

79
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,560
Level four!

80
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:26,700
Huh?

81
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,140
It would seem you missed.

82
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:29,900
Ugh!

83
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:31,160
Who cares?

84
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,020
I don't need you to tell me that!

85
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,800
Why don't you do something useful

86
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,560
and figure out a wish for me instead?

87
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:38,480
My wish?

88
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:40,540
Here it comes!

89
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,580
Try not to flip out and wet yourself

90
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,240
when I see your dirty little secret!

91
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,580
Hurry it up, Piraluck!

92
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:49,580
I haven't had my dose of butthurt babies today!

93
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,300
There's nothing.

94
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:51,880
Huh?

95
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,540
What's your deal?

96
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:56,360
You Elrigs can't, like, malfunction, can you?

97
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,500
She has...

98
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,640
no wish.

99
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:03,920
Yeah, she's right.

100
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:05,700
I admit it.

101
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,600
I don't have a wish yet.

102
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:07,980
Huh!

103
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:08,900
What?

104
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,500
Let me get this straight.

105
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,240
You're battling as a selector,

106
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:14,120
but you have nothing you want to fight for?

107
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,040
That is, like, so messed up!

108
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,300
What are you, a sociopath or something?

109
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:20,540
All the selectors are, like,

110
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:22,680
do or die when it comes to their wishes!

111
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,660
And you're just crapping all over that

112
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,580
so you can have fun?

113
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:27,300
That is sick, yo. Sick!

114
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,480
Participating as a selector

115
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,820
without having a wish

116
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,440
is more than just wrong.

117
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:33,740
It's blasphemy.

118
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,740
I don't care what you say.

119
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:36,480
Huh?

120
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,320
Just means I have nothing to lose.

121
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:41,280
So you can't scare me!

122
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:43,060
Argora!

123
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,220
Toma!

124
00:05:45,220 --> 00:06:01,300
What the hell is wrong with you?

125
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:04,700
You just said you don't have a wish.

126
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,540
So tell me.

127
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:10,220
Why the hell are you trying to stomp all over mine?

128
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,760
No, that's not why I did this.

129
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,340
I just wanted you to...

130
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,920
Don't give me that crap!

131
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,140
You just wanted to see me suffer, didn't you?

132
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,740
And I bet you enjoyed it!

133
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,460
Hold on a sec!

134
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:45,100
Let's stop.

135
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,100
Met with Ruko and Yuzuki.

136
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,600
Played Wii Cross at the library.

137
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,700
On our way back, we bought stuffed dumplings.

138
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,200
Ruko... and... Yuzuki...

139
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,500
Ichui!

140
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,700
What happened?

141
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:17,100
The words are disappearing!

142
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,100
What?

143
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,100
My notes!

144
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,100
Everything I wrote is just fading away!

145
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:24,100
I don't know why!

146
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,100
I can't remember!

147
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:28,100
Ichui.

148
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:32,100
Is Akira late again?

149
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:35,100
Yonah, have you heard from her?

150
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:36,100
Not today.

151
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:39,100
You know what? Forget it. I don't even care anymore.

152
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:42,100
Right? She's off the cover for next issue. Good riddance.

153
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,100
Better yet, why don't we just drop her for a while?

154
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,100
Sounds good.

155
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:47,100
Good.

156
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,100
Yonah.

157
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,100
Yonah.

158
00:07:53,100 --> 00:08:02,100
You have the scent of battle on you. Or the stink of defeat, at least.

159
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:05,100
That reminds me.

160
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:08,100
Do you remember that poor girl who battled Yonah a while back?

161
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:11,100
That was her second battle. And her second defeat.

162
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:15,100
In other words, she was one loss away from bidding farewell to her wish.

163
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:20,100
Knowing that she was backed into a corner, you approached her.

164
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:24,100
And you sweet-talked her into another battle with a free win as bait.

165
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:29,100
And as she sat there struggling to breathe, suffering from the illness that ravaged her body,

166
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:34,100
you betrayed her. You crushed a dying girl for your own gain.

167
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:39,100
And it wasn't just her wish, but her very life that you snatched away from her.

168
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:45,100
What does it matter to you? I can run my battles however the hell I want, can't I? Can't I?

169
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:50,100
Yes, you certainly can. Though I do have to question the effectiveness of your little method,

170
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:53,100
since you lost so badly to the next girl Yonah beat.

171
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:57,100
That's why you stopped feeding off Yonah's scraps, isn't it?

172
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:02,100
And why you started picking on the rookie selectors instead.

173
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:05,100
Tell me how that worked out for you again?

174
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:09,100
Yet another loss. Pathetic.

175
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:14,100
I don't want your filthy hands disgracing any more selector battles.

176
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:15,100
Screw you!

177
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:18,100
Your wish is to see Yonah's life ruined, right?

178
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:21,100
I know you want to beat her.

179
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:26,100
So why don't you challenge her to a battle already? Why do you avoid it when she's right here?

180
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:29,100
I told you! I can battle however the hell I want to!

181
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:32,100
And either way, when I get my wish, you're going down!

182
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,100
Thank you very much.

183
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:36,100
Huh?

184
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:39,100
Oh, looks like Yuko's here for the shoot.

185
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:42,100
Are you kidding? But I thought me and Yonah were doing the cover today.

186
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:45,100
You don't have a shoot today. Sorry.

187
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,100
Huh? What?

188
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:50,100
While you were so occupied looking for rookie selectors to pick on,

189
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:53,100
you seem to have lost your coveted position as a model.

190
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:57,100
Aw, are you gonna cry?

191
00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:00,100
You tried too hard to ruin Yonah's career,

192
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,100
and ended up ruining your own.

193
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:05,100
I don't want to keep them waiting.

194
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,100
Goodbye, loser.

195
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:16,100
I don't care about my career, or my life, or anything as long as I can ruin yours!

196
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:20,100
I'll tear you apart with my own two hands if I have to, you bitch!

197
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:25,100
Time to put her out of her misery.

198
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:35,100
It doesn't seem like you have a fever, but you're still not feeling well?

199
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:38,100
No. My head feels like it's gonna explode.

200
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:42,100
I see. Well, I'll call the school for you and tell them what's wrong.

201
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:45,100
You just lay there and take it easy, all right?

202
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:52,100
Now I'm making Grandma worry again.

203
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:53,100
Ruuu!

204
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,100
You! And I bet you enjoyed it!

205
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,100
Why do I like battles so much?

206
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:03,100
Why do I keep wanting to have them?

207
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:07,100
I know all the horrible things that'll happen if I continue playing.

208
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,100
But still, I can't stop!

209
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,100
You don't have to cry, Ruu!

210
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,100
You know what?

211
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:16,100
It makes Thomas so happy to see you have fun battling!

212
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:18,100
So don't be sad!

213
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,100
We can have lots of battles and-

214
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:21,100
No, stop it!

215
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,100
Please, Ruu!

216
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:28,100
Hey, Kazuki. You aren't too busy today, are you?

217
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,100
Yeah, let's hang.

218
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:31,100
Okay, sounds good.

219
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:33,100
Didn't think it'd say yes.

220
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,100
Cool, we can grab some grub.

221
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:36,100
If you like curry, I know a place.

222
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,100
Let's go!

223
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:39,100
Can we talk for a sec?

224
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:47,100
Nothing personal, but you and Kazuki are kind of leaving a bad impression on people.

225
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,100
What?

226
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:51,100
Like the way you two always hang out is bordering on creepy.

227
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:53,100
Geez, could you be any more blunt?

228
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:58,100
Anyway, don't look so upset. We're not teasing. We're actually really worried.

229
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,100
You're worried?

230
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:03,100
We've been hearing all those awful rumors about you two, so we came to give you some advice.

231
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:06,100
Do you think I'm stupid? What's it matter to you?

232
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:13,100
All right, fine. I'm actually worried about Kazuki. You, I couldn't care less about.

233
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:18,100
When I see you stalking him all day, it just makes me feel sorry for him.

234
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:23,100
Yeah, it's awkward. Maybe you don't realize it, but Kazuki's actually a pretty popular guy.

235
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,100
But now there's all these weird rumors because you...

236
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:28,100
Geez, nice attitude.

237
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,100
Guess what they say about them is true. Ew.

238
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,100
Now, now.

239
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,100
Damn it.

240
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:40,100
Yuzuki.

241
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:41,100
Don't talk to me!

242
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:49,100
What's wrong with them? Everyone's so stupid. They're the creepy ones, not me.

243
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,100
Howdy-do!

244
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:57,100
Ugh! I knew it! You're a selector, aren't you?

245
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:01,100
Yay! I finally met one! I'm the awesomest!

246
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,100
Ugh, selectors are so hard to find!

247
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:10,100
Oh, by the way, my name's Chiori. So, can we have a battle already? Pretty, pretty, please?

248
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:13,100
Listen, kid. Here's a little secret.

249
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,100
Ooh!

250
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:20,100
If you lose three selector battles, something unspeakably terrible happens to you.

251
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,100
Yuzuki.

252
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,100
Duh! I already knew that!

253
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:26,100
Heh! It's all written down right here!

254
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:30,100
Huh? A novel? Of Wecross?

255
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:37,100
Yep! So yeah, after your third loss, the magical Wecross factors inside your body go crazy and blow up like a hot air balloon!

256
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,100
Until kaboom! Guts flying everywhere!

257
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:42,100
Pretty scary!

258
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:44,100
Wait, that's not...

259
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:49,100
That's why selectors are so cool, right? They put their lives on the line to fight for their wishes!

260
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,100
Uh-huh.

261
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,100
Huh?

262
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:57,100
Hey, sorry. My girl here's a little soft in the head, you see?

263
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:01,100
Ugh! Eldora! She'll see how hard my head is when we battle!

264
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:09,100
Now, back to what I was saying before! I'm offering my commemorative first battle to you, Miss Selector on the playground!

265
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,100
I don't know.

266
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:16,100
Oh, stop it! You're too much, Kazuki!

267
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,100
It's not that big a deal.

268
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,100
You don't have to go home yet, do you?

269
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:22,100
Uh, no. I guess not.

270
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:25,100
Oh, good. There's still a bunch of stuff I need to ask you.

271
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:29,100
Come on, let's battle! Please, for me!

272
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,100
Fine.

273
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,100
Yuzuki!

274
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,100
Let's do this.

275
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:38,100
Yay! Finally!

276
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:40,100
It's battle time!

277
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:48,100
Hey, sweetie, I've got to step out for a bit. Try to take it easy, okay?

278
00:14:48,100 --> 00:15:00,100
It's strange. I feel like I've been searching for something, but I can't remember what it is.

279
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:10,100
I just know that if I can't have it, nothing matters. And there's no reason to be alive anymore.

280
00:15:10,100 --> 00:15:11,100
The bitter, bitter taste has defeat!

281
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:28,100
Yep, she's strong. Way stronger than you, Chiori. Sorry about that. Bet that was a waste of your time, huh?

282
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:34,100
You're so rude! Learn the rules. In our first fight, the heroine has to lose, okay?

283
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,100
Yeah, I'll be sure to write that one down.

284
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:42,100
Oh, here, give this a read. It's good. We'll meet again for sure, right?

285
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:44,100
Fairly well, selector!

286
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,100
Yup!

287
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,100
You alright?

288
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,100
Well, I finally won.

289
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:56,100
Yes.

290
00:15:57,100 --> 00:16:00,100
All it takes are three losses, and my wish is gone forever.

291
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:04,100
But there's no telling how many times I have to win if I want it to come true.

292
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,100
Isn't that the way it works?

293
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:09,100
Only when the conditions are met.

294
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:13,100
The conditions, huh? That's kind of cryptic, don't you think?

295
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:16,100
I'm sure you'll tell me after it's too late.

296
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:21,100
All I've thought about is winning, but now I wonder what would happen if my wish was corrupted.

297
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:26,100
Maybe Kazuki would drift away from me?

298
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,100
No, it has to be worse than that.

299
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:33,100
I bet he would end up hating me, and I'd never see him again for the rest of my life.

300
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,100
He was with that girl. I wonder where they went.

301
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,100
Stop it.

302
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:43,100
Maybe they went to Momoka's place to pick out cards.

303
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:46,100
I think his friends are still new to the game.

304
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,100
That used to be our thing we did together, you know?

305
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,100
Yuzuki, listen to me.

306
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,100
Then maybe they'll go to a movie.

307
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:55,100
Stop by the food court afterwards to try out their new decks.

308
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,100
Then they'll get a snack.

309
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,100
And exchange numbers.

310
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:01,100
Laugh and smile.

311
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,100
Walk home together.

312
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:04,100
Yuzuki!

313
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:06,100
I hate it.

314
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:12,100
If they're gonna take Kazuki away from me, I'd rather just die now and get it over with!

315
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:19,100
No matter how upset you may be, you should never say something like that.

316
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,100
You don't think I'm serious?

317
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,100
I hate you for lying to me!

318
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:28,100
But I know… I know I need you for my wish to come true.

319
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,100
I'm not stupid!

320
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:34,100
I know Akira made a fool of me, but I beat that new girl no problem!

321
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:39,100
If I still have a shot at becoming an eternal girl, then my wish can come true!

322
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:45,100
Kazuki can be mine forever, and he won't be taken away from me!

323
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,100
Listen!

324
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:51,100
I am your Elrig through thick and thin.

325
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:56,100
I will always follow you, wherever fate takes us.

326
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:04,100
When I was living with Mom, I don't think I asked for too much.

327
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,100
I wasn't spoiled.

328
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:12,100
She always wanted to be left alone, so I tried not to bother her, but…

329
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:17,100
I don't know what Ruko's thinking. There's something… scary about her.

330
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:23,100
I never knew how or why I was scaring my Mom, and that made me afraid too.

331
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:30,100
But I'm fine as long as I have Grandma and Ayumu with me, and I try not to ask for too much from them.

332
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:36,100
I don't want to scare anyone, or bother anyone, or hurt anyone ever again.

333
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,100
But now…

334
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:45,100
You know what? It makes Thomas so happy to see you have fun battling!

335
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,100
No! No, please!

336
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:59,100
Where do you get off acting like a victim?

337
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,100
You just wanted to see me suffer.

338
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,100
And I bet you enjoyed it, didn't you?

339
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,100
Roo?

340
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,100
Wake up, Roo.

341
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:12,100
There's a phone call for you.

342
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:16,100
I explained that you were asleep, but apparently it's something important.

343
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:18,100
What?

344
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,100
Oh…

345
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,100
Oh…

346
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:27,100
Sorry to just call out of the blue. Do you like parfaits?

347
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,100
I probably should have asked before I ordered, but I hope it's okay.

348
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:32,100
Ah, thanks.

349
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:47,100
Hitae usually gets the kind with candied chestnuts. This one looks awfully good. I'll have to come back here with her sometime.

350
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:48,100
So what did you…

351
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:49,100
I looked through Hitae's phone. She had your number and Yuzuki's in her contacts.

352
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:51,100
Huh?

353
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,100
You must think I'm a horrible mother for snooping, but I also found this. Here.

354
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,100
Hold on. Is this the notebook she kept on WeCross?

355
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:55,100
You've seen it?

356
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,100
Uh, yes, ma'am.

357
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:59,100
Hitae can't read it anymore. She said that all the words were disappearing. She also tells me she doesn't remember you.

358
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,100
Huh!

359
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:02,100
Today, Ruko and Yuzuki had your number and Yuzuki's in her contacts.

360
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,100
Huh?

361
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:08,100
You must think I'm a horrible mother for snooping, but I also found this. Here.

362
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:11,100
Hold on. Is this the notebook she kept on WeCross?

363
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,100
You've seen it?

364
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:13,100
Uh, yes, ma'am.

365
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:21,100
Hitae can't read it anymore. She said that all the words were disappearing. She also tells me she doesn't remember you.

366
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,100
Huh?

367
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:50,100
Today, Ruko and Yuzuki and I bought a matching set of scrunchies. They both look really cute when they put them in their hair. They said I was cute, too. I'll have to take their word for it. I was already so happy, but having the chance to be together with them, sharing all of our fun and joy, it was just wonderful. Friendship truly is a beautiful thing.

368
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:59,100
She was so happy to make new friends. She wouldn't stop talking about you. I don't know what went wrong.

369
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:06,100
Ruko, please, if there's anything you can tell me about what happened, even if you had an argument or she got angry at you over something, I don't care.

370
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:11,100
I promise I'm not trying to blame you, but it seems like something just snapped and I need to know what caused it.

371
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:17,100
Ruko, tell me.

372
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:33,100
Ito, I lost three times. I was just having fun battling with my friends. We didn't know what would happen if we lost. I mean, our wish had already come true. We didn't know it would get corrupted like that.

373
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:39,100
Ruko, I don't... Please, just explain what this is about. Ruko, wait!

374
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:53,100
I feel so lost. Everything is wrong. I don't know what to do anymore. Help me!

375
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,100
We are let's see.

376
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,100
Ruko, hold me!

377
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:03,100
Ruko, hold me!

378
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:05,100
Ruko, hold me!

379
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,100
possess me.

380
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:08,100
Ruko, hold me!

381
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:11,100
Ruko…

382
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:41,080
Thank you.

383
00:22:41,100 --> 00:23:11,080
Thank you.

384
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:13,100
Thank you.

